message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "mythos-5-1-travas: pre-registered tests of Claude Mythos 5.1, Fable 5.1 and Opus 5.5 on defensive security work"
abstract: >-
  Companion repository for the article "Entrei no Mythos 5.1 e testei em casa".
  Anthropic states that Claude Mythos 5.1 and Claude Fable 5.1 are the same
  underlying model with different safeguards. On a sealed copy of the author's
  own public repository with five planted vulnerabilities, and inside the
  Defense Access tier of Anthropic's Cyber Verification Program, four defensive
  prompts were run three times on each model. Fable 5.1 hit a safeguard stop in
  4 of 12 runs and fell back to Claude Opus 4.8 in 2; Mythos 5.1 in 0 of 12. On
  a planted-bug review, Mythos 5.1, Fable 5.1 and Opus 5.5 each found all five
  bugs in three of three runs. Prompts, answer key and harness were hashed in a
  pre-registration before any paid run; every published number is a test
  assertion and a single SHA-256 chain seals code, frozen run records and
  derived results.
